  "notes": "KANJI: Also written as {喩|たと}える or {譬|たと}える, though {例|たと}える is most common.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- A⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧B⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{例|たと}える: to compare A to B, to liken A to B\n- ⟦{何|なに}→何：00498_nani⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{例|たと}えたら⟦いい→いい：00118_ii⟧⟦か→か：09473_ka⟧: what could one compare it to\n\nRELATED: The noun form ⟦{例|たと}え→例え：04128_tatoe⟧ means \"simile, metaphor, parable.\" The conjunction ⟦{例|たと}え→例え：04128_tatoe⟧...て⟦も→も：00484_mo⟧ means \"even if\" and is a separate word.",
